# Native PostgreSQL operator setup ONLY. This example contains no credentials.
# Edit the already-created, Git-ignored .env.foundation.local; do not overwrite it
# with this example, since replacing a file can replace its restricted Windows ACL.
# Keep exactly these three assignments in the private file. Use single quotes
# around values containing spaces, #, $ or Windows backslashes. If a value
# contains a single quote, use a compatible Node env-file quoted representation.
# Never add VITE_, NODE_OPTIONS, extra variables, commands or connection URLs.

YTRACE_PRODUCTION_DB_PASSWORD='REPLACE_WITH_DATABASE_PASSWORD'
YTRACE_PRODUCTION_DB_CA_FILE='C:\REPLACE_WITH_ABSOLUTE_PATH\trusted-ca.crt'
YTRACE_PRODUCTION_DB_CA_SHA256='REPLACE_WITH_INDEPENDENTLY_TRUSTED_64_HEX_SHA256'

# Password: enter the reset PostgreSQL account password; not an API/service key.
# CA file: existing local certificate from an authenticated trusted source.
# CA SHA-256: independently reviewed fingerprint of those exact bytes.
# A matching file hash alone does not establish certificate provenance.
# Never print/upload the private file or pass its values as command arguments.
# Edit/save it in place; verify Windows ACLs again if an editor replaces the file.

# Node 22.14.0 is installed and supports --env-file. It loads variables only in
# the child Node process. Existing same-name environment variables take priority:
# use a fresh PowerShell or clear ONLY these three process variables first.
# From the repository root, after filling the private file:
# node --env-file=.env.foundation.local scripts/security/verify-foundation-environment.mjs
# Stop unless verification reports PASS. The validator never connects to a DB.
# The NEXT task may run the existing READ-ONLY commands:
# node --env-file=.env.foundation.local docs/production-security/storage-cutover/diagnostics/20261011T125750Z/native-postgres-readonly-probe.mjs
# node --env-file=.env.foundation.local docs/production-security/storage-cutover/native-runner-20261011T132539Z/native-foundation-runner.mjs --preflight
# Preflight also requires fresh independent control-plane evidence at the fixed
# ignored path documented in the existing operator procedure. No installation
# authorization is needed or created for read-only verification.

# Frontend isolation: these names have no VITE_ prefix. The Vite config refuses
# foundation mode and refuses inherited foundation variables; never load this
# file for npm/Vite/frontend builds. Keep it outside src/ and public/.
# Native TLS, identity and catalog readiness are NOT established by this setup.
